{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Subscribing","type":"heading","anchor":"Subscribing","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for try await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop over the subject","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. From then on, every value sent is buffered for that consumer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until it is consumed, so a consumer that is slower than the sender still sees every value, in order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Values sent while there are no subscribers are discarded; they are never replayed to a later consumer.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Starting a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that iterates the subject does not mean it has subscribed yet. If values must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not be missed, wait until the consumer has subscribed before sending, for example with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important"},{"text":"Example","type":"heading","ancho